<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Everything an assistant knows about you had to arrive somehow. Notes are
    that: the facts, the context, the things you'd have to explain again
    every time otherwise.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your daughter's teacher's name. The plumber who was good. What the
    consultant said in March. The reason you decided against the other
    quote. Small things, individually forgettable, which together are the
    difference between software that knows your situation and software that
    asks you to describe it.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What they're for</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Written by you") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Typed in a few seconds, tagged to whichever parts of your life they
        touch, and findable later by searching for a word you remember.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Written by the app") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Every letter the app drafts and every explanation it produces is
        saved here too. Your appeal, your budget, the plain-language read of
        your policy — kept, editable, and yours.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Read back when it matters") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Because notes are filed by area, a tool working on your insurance
        already has what you wrote about your insurance. That's why the
        forms are short.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Testable, if you like") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        A note about something you're learning can be turned into a quick
        quiz on the spot, which is a surprisingly effective way to find out
        whether reading it counted as knowing it.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">This is the part worth owning</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Models will keep getting better and keep getting replaced. What accrues
    is this layer — years of context that makes any model useful to you
    specifically. It's a file on your disk, it belongs to you, and it's the
    reason swapping the model out costs you nothing.
  </p>
</section>
